OrionLayer open fix 121 — the Fleets screen's move preview on the wire
=====================================================================

Work order 406. orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on top
of open fix 120 and its README row. Not on `orionlayer-local`. In
src/ext/ext_api.cpp only, under ORION2RE_EXT (the file is compiled only
with it).

The Fleets screen prints a move preview: the strip under the inset map says
where the selected ships would get to (Print_Fltscrn_Scanned_Star_Name,
flt2.cpp:338-522: H 0x67, 0x69/0x6A, 0x6B/0x6C, 0x21, 0x6E, 0x6F/0x70, 0xEB,
0x73) and Draw_Fltscrn_Ship_Destination_Lines (flt1.cpp:130-170) colours the
selected stack's line to the hovered star green or red. Both read
g_ship_move_info, which flt2.cpp:349-354 fills on hover with
SHIPMOVE::Ships_Try_To_Move_To over Build_Fltscrn_Ship_List's ships (the big
icons with selected != 0, in display order, flt2.cpp:863-890) unless
FLT1::relocate_button_mode is 1. FMOV (open fix 48) carried that verdict only
for the galaxy map's fleet box (SCREEN_MAIN).

The change. SerializeState writes "FMOV" on SCREEN_FLEET too, before FILM,
in the layout of open fix 48 (version byte 1, int16 star count, uint8 record
size 14, one s_ship_move_info per star) — the verdict is made at every star
into a local struct, as the galaxy map's block does, the global untouched.
The ships are gathered as Build_Fltscrn_Ship_List gathers them but without
calling it, which opens a "Too many ships" box when the list is full. On this
screen the block is ALWAYS written: with a selection and the relocate mode off
the count is NUM_STARS and the records follow; with none selected, in RELOCATE
mode or with a full list the count is 0 and no record follows (the original's
else branch, flt2.cpp:355-381). So a client reads "FMOV present on the Fleets
screen" as "this engine knows the question" and "count 0" as "no verdict:
the strip names the star".

Live: UNVERIFIED — see doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md entry 121. Built on the
scratch clone `~/claude/clones/406_orion2re` (`linux-debug`, ORION2RE_EXT on);
a misspelt call (`Ships_Try_To_Move_ToX`) is refused by the compiler.

